<figure id="A2.T9" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 9: </span><span id="A2.T9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Detailed performance comparison on SIMPLER-WidowX <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2024</a>)</cite></span>. We report both the task success rate and the grasp success rate (%) over 24 trials on 4 pick-and-place tasks. Results for our methods are averaged over 3 random seeds, while baseline results are taken from the SIMPLER paper <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2024</a>)</cite> and the respective original papers <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Qu et al., 2025</a>)</cite>. <math id="A2.T9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dagger" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>†</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dagger</annotation></semantics></math> indicates reproduced performance, and <math id="A2.T9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="*" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∗</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">*</annotation></semantics></math> indicates results with additional joint training before applying our test-time scaling framework.</figcaption>
